Bubbling out of the ground here is a naturally occurring spring.  It makes a 
soft, musical sound as the water trickles over the stones and filters down to
nourish the surrounding garden.  Emananting from the water is a faint light as
well, such that you imagine that your eyes are playing tricks on you.  You are
tempted to drink from this spring, but a sharp intuition tells you that this is
not the best of ideas. A gate to the east seems oddly neglected in such an 
immaculate garden as this, though its beauty is barely affected by the onset
of what appears to be many years of overgrown vines.
